WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.410
Video game fans have plenty of questions about
the movie adaptation of "Uncharted."

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.890
For one, did Tom Holland really pull off the
role of Nathan Drake?

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.220
Even after seeing the film, some questions
will linger.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.540
Keep watching for the biggest.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.559
After being caught breaking and entering and
threatened with prison, Nate's brother Sam

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:18.159
escapes from the orphanage where the brothers
live.

00:00:18.159 --> 00:00:22.669
Sam promises he'll come back, but he never
does, leaving Nate to wonder where Sam went.

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:26.869
Nate's mentor Victor "Sully" Sullivan admits
that Sam used to be his treasure-hunting partner,

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:30.580
yet he avoids talking about Sam's fate for
most of the film.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.990
"I think you're here because of your brother."

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.180
"Wait, you know my brother Sam?"

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.920
Eventually it becomes clear that Sully and
his sometimes ally Chloe believe Sam is dead.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.230
The mercenary Braddock even indicates she's
the one who killed him.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.170
At the end of the film, though, there's a
brief scene set in a dingy prison that indicates

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.360
Sam is still kicking.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.890
We see a man writing a postcard, the form
of communication he used to reach out to Nate.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.800
But where is he, and how did he survive if
Sully, Chloe, and Braddock all thought they

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.800
saw him die?

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.370
There are several tantalizing ways that Nate
and Sully could learn about Sam's situation.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.050
They could find out from a third party and
rescue him.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.201
Nate could find out Sully secretly knows the
truth about Sam, leading to a rift.

00:01:04.201 --> 00:01:08.200
Or Sam could escape and seek out the pair
in some unexpected way.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.850
There's plenty of fodder for a sequel.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:15.070
"Uncharted" makes it seem as though Santiago
Moncada is the film's main villain, but when

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.970
Braddock, the mercenary he hired, kills him
midway through the film, she becomes the true

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:19.970
antagonist.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.590
Moncada was willing to do whatever it took
to find and claim Magellan's treasure, but

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.340
he didn't like to get his hands dirty.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.840
Braddock, on the other hand, is more than
happy to get her hands dirty, and has a band

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.210
of goons who seem to share her cutthroat impulses.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:33.160
That doesn't mean she's a great villain.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.930
Her motivations mostly seem to revolve around
the desire for a massive payday.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:41.340
Still, she keeps the film's fight scenes interesting,
including in the final fight on one of Magellan's

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.340
ships.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.800
When she loses the fight and falls into the
ocean, that ship ends up crashing into the

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.330
water on top of her.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.630
Given the circumstances, it seems like Braddock
must have died on contact, but there are plenty

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:55.000
of movies that have made it seem like the
villain is dead only to resurrect them in

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.000
the sequel.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.210
If, say, Braddock was a strong swimmer, she
could have gotten away before the ship hit

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.550
the sea and we wouldn't have seen it.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:05.230
The movie's mid-credits sequence sets up Nate
and Sully's next adventure.

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:08.500
Nate meets a man with an eyepatch to make
a trade to acquire a map that will lead to

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.080
Nazi treasure, although it's never clear what,
specifically, he's hoping to find.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:17.320
In World War II, the Nazis confiscated and
looted all kinds of valuable art and artifacts,

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.730
so it wouldn't be all that surprising if Nate
and Sully decided to go after one of those

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:21.730
treasures.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:25.520
Besides, Nazis come up a couple times during
the "Uncharted" games, so it's possible their

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.410
mention in the mid-credits scene is an indication
that, although this "Uncharted" film told

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:33.810
an original story, the plot of the sequel
will take its cues from the plot of one of

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:34.810
the games.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:38.350
Either way, going up against Nazis is a popular
trope in action-adventure films.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.550
Everyone from Indiana Jones to Captain America
have done it, so perhaps it's no surprise

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:45.810
that Nathan Drake and Sully would do so as
well.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.700
The man that Nate meets in the mid-credits
scene references his boss during their exchange.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.850
We don't know much about this boss, but one
of the things he requests in exchange for

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:56.000
the Nazi map is the ring Nate wears on a strap
around his neck.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.420
The ring has sentimental value for Nate: It
was originally Sam's, and Sam gave it to Nate

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:01.580
when he left.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.290
Yet as Nate points out, it has no real-world
value.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.450
The man with the eyepatch's boss isn't seeking
financial gain, though.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.970
His boss wants it because it has value to
Nate.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:13.010
It seems as though this unseen boss could
be an interesting antagonist.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:16.870
Of course, it's unclear whether he will be
the main villain in the next movie, as Nate

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:20.020
and Sully could find themselves racing against
someone else to claim the treasure.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:24.120
Yet the fact that this boss is still unknown
indicates he could be a big player in the

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.120
next film.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.000
Could this be a villain from the "Uncharted"
games?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.580
Or maybe it's Sam himself.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.959
After all, if Sam escaped from prison and
amassed his own gang, it could explain why

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:36.780
the man with the eyepatch said his boss wanted
Nate's ring.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.130
In the last moments of the mid-credits scene,
Sully shows up to help Nate when the meeting

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.200
with the man with the eyepatch goes south.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.310
After Sully gets the situation under control,
Nate and Sully leave together.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.880
They bicker about Sully's delayed arrival
until they see something that stops them in

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:49.980
their tracks.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.230
The final second of the film shows them looking
dumbfounded.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.239
But what do they see?

00:03:54.239 --> 00:03:57.830
It's entirely possible that they've run into
a new character or characters that we won't

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:58.930
meet until the sequel.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:01.700
Or they may have encountered a character we're
familiar with.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.880
Perhaps Braddock really is alive and has finally
hunted them down.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.400
Or perhaps this is the point where Sam reveals
he's still among the living.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.380
There are a ton of possibilities, but without
an idea of the potential story for the sequel,

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.819
it's hard to narrow them down.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.449
"What else aren't you telling me?"

00:04:16.449 --> 00:04:19.680
Sully summons Chloe Fraser when he and Nate
first arrive in Spain.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.300
Even though Chloe initially antagonizes them,
they eventually team up to track down a map

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.379
to help them find Magellan's gold.

00:04:25.379 --> 00:04:29.400
Nate and Sully quickly learn she wasn't entirely
trustworthy; she was actually working for

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.809
Moncada, and she regularly makes it clear
that she doesn't trust anyone.

00:04:32.809 --> 00:04:37.409
Even so, she eventually helps them reclaim
the artifacts they need from Moncada's plane.

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:41.419
By the time Nate figures out the location
of the treasure, he knows he can't trust Chloe.

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:45.300
So he leaves a set of fake coordinates just
in case she takes off before he wakes up.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.150
Unfortunately for Chloe, she takes the bait,
which means instead of finding the gold with

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:50.960
him, she goes on a wild goose chase.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:55.150
The movie gives no indication of what that
means for her relationship with Nate or Sully,

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.710
leaving open the question of what could happen
if she ever meets up with them again.

